   Plants and Receiving Waters in Urban Areas (INTERURBA II), LISBON,
   PORTUGAL, FEB 19-22, 2001},
Abstract = {The sewer system for the Greater Copenhagen area covers an area of 4460
   ha contributing to the runoff. The total area serves in total 8
   municipalities, however it is dominated by the areas in the City of
   Copenhagen proper. The catchments merge into interceptors, which feed
   two large treatment plants. The effluent from the two treatment plants
   discharges during dry weather to Oresund, the sound between Denmark and
   Sweden. This large system has been analysed for selected scenarios with
   respect to handling runoff in an optimal way in order to minimise the
   loads on the most sensitive receiving waters and optimising treatment
   plant performance.},
