   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc;
   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {This paper describes a method in which sustainability objectives were
   translated into a short list of performance measures or effects through
   public consultation and the weightings of these effects were determined
   by the analysis of a stated preference survey in which respondents were
   asked to choose between development alternatives described in terms of
   eight effects. The model on which this paper is based achieved adj
   rho(2) of 0.283 and found the weightings for the effects to be 0.0237
   per long term job created, -0.4588 per sick day experienced per person
   per year, -0.0016 per litre of potable water used per household per day,
   0.2573 per hectare of valuable natural environment retained and -0.0002
   per rand spent annually to maintain the sustainability techniques that
   were implemented. The three effects that were not included because of
   poor t-scores were the kg of household waste sent to landfill per week,
   the kWh of electricity consumed per household per month, and the hours
   spent by the household per week improving its sustainability.},
