   NOV 21-24, 1998},
Organization = {Decis Sci Inst},
Abstract = {State and federal regulators have turned to economic incentives, which
   force offending companies to include the costs of polluting the
   environment in their production processes. In order to maximize profits
   companies can alter their operations to avoid paying the associated
   fees. I sent surveys to environmental managers in order to describe
   corporate responses to and perceptions of the various types of
   regulatory policies that can be used to help eliminate or control toxic
   emissions. In addition, I examined the company-specific factors
   associated with these corporate responses.},
