   Brazilian Assoc Ergon; Brazilian Assoc Occupat Hyg; Brazilian Assoc Prod
   Engn},
Abstract = {The construction industry is a growing sector in countries that are
   prosperous in economic development, leading to the new studies that
   drive this sector. Thus, it appears that the buildings have a great
   relationship with thermal environment, due to their constant exposure to
   those factors. This can influence the productivity of workers,
   compromising the execution of construction. This paper aims at
   investigating the influence of the thermal environment in building at
   elevated heights, establishing a relationship with productivity. For
   that, was done a sistematic bibliographic research in this area trying
   to stablish the stat of the art starting from the papers published in
   the last ten years. It appears that there is a relationship between the
   subjects studied, although most of the survey does not include all the
   issues.},
