   UNIV, BLOOMINGTON, IN, JUN 02-05, 2002},
Abstract = {Homeowners' preferences for vegetation near their homes and defensible
   space options are documented for wildfire prone areas in Florida and
   Minnesota through 80 indepth interviews and home site visits. The
   dominant preference for ``natural{''} landscapes is articulated as
   valuing vegetated views, wildlife, recreation, quiet, solitude, and
   privacy Homeowners recognize wildfire risk but vary in their perceptions
   of effective wildfire prevention measures and actions taken to reduce
   their risk. Most of these homeowners are supportive of prescribed burns,
   especially if fire experts who understand the local ecology and fire
   behavior conduct the burns.},
