Abstract = {The thermal expansion of concrete elements concerns both monolithic and
   prefabricated structures. Inappropriate design of dilation segments may
   cause minor but even larger failures. Critical environment factors are
   temperature-changing operations, such as unheated underground garages,
   where temperature fluctuations may occur depending on the exterior
   conditions. This paper numerically and experimentally analyses the
   thermal deformation of selected girders in the underground garages and
   the consequent structure failures, their causes, possible prevention and
   appropriate remediation.},
