   CONFERENCE},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {605-614},
Note = {Beijing International Environmental Technology Conference, Beijing,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 16-19, 2009},
Organization = {Univ Sci \& Technol Beijing; Water \& Wastewater Engn Magazine
   Publishing; Univ Appl Sci Stuttgart; Tech Univ Hamburg, Harburg;
   Stockholm Environm Inst; China Node Sustainable Sanitat; Beijing Environ
   Syst Co},
Abstract = {A large portion of urban water use in China goes to watering landscape.
   Landscape water can improve the residential quarters of the natural
   environment, to meet people close to nature and the pursuit of health.
   Landscape water conservation is an important issue if the problem of
   having sufficient supplies to meet increasing demand while minimizing
   environmental impacts is to be addresses. However, common
   recommendations for addressing landscape water conservation are too
   simple to deal with the great variability in urban residential
   landscape. So how could maintain the residential landscape water in
   healthy state is the problem which must be solves in the landscape water
   design. The study at the center of this dissertation was designed to
   address questions of how to best predict and promote landscape water
   conservation. We analysis landscape water conservation about landscape
   water current situation; water source analysis; water balance and
   protection method. Understanding the interactions among the above
   elements in this framework is vital to achieving landscape water
   conservation goals. The findings from this research have implications
   for better understanding the human-technology-landscape system and for
   designing more effective landscape water conservation programs. The
   theoretical framework presented gives urban landscape water managers new
   tools and approaches to devise simple recommendations for improving
   landscape water use efficiency that take into account the high
   variability in urban residential landscape. Based on the detailed
   analysis of the content of the ecological settlements water environment
   systems. How to maintain the cell within the body of water in a healthy
   state of the landscape as the landscape design of water an issue that
   must be addressed in this paper on the ecological residential district
   of the composition of the water environment system on the basis of a
   detailed analysis in order to a villa in Tianjin Wuqing residential
   district, for example, combined with its local natural landscape, the
   surrounding environment, and climatic features, landscape and water
   quality projects to build and maintain the design must take into account
   the factors discussed.},
