Abstract = {The aim of this study was to examine the relationship between emotional
   intelligence (EI) and coping styles with stress in a sample of students.
   Four hundred and thirteen students (140 boys, 273 girls) were included
   in this study. All participants completed the Emotional Intelligence
   Scale (EIS) and the Tehran Coping Styles Scale (TCSS). The results
   revealed that EI was positively associated with problem-focused and
   positive emotional focused coping styles, and negatively associated with
   negative emotional focused coping style. EI is supposed to influence
   coping strrategies through management and regulation of emotions,
   utilization and facilitation of emotions, and apprisal of emotions.},
