   ELECTR NETWORK, SEP 26-OCT 02, 2020},
Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers Geoscience
   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {Digital Surface Model (DSM) provides the detailed structure and geometry
   of an urban environment. This paper proposes an approach of using a type
   of image-to-image translation deep learning model called cycle
   consistent adversarial networks for reconstructing DSM from monocular
   aerial imagery. The cycleGAN architecture consisted of two generators
   with an encoder-decoder network with skip connections and two
   discriminators that punishes structures at the scale of patches. The
   cycleGAN objective function was adapted for training on paired images.
   The evaluation was performed using mean square error (MSE) and zero
   normalized cross-correlation (ZNCC) for errors in reconstruction. cGAN
   model was considered as a baseline model for comparison of the proposed
   approach. The results using the proposed approach confirmed a higher
   reconstruction accuracy than previous studies that utilized conditional
   GAN.},
