   SCIENCE (REES 2017)},
Series = {IOP Conference Series-Earth and Environmental Science},
Year = {2017},
Volume = {64},
Note = {International Symposium on Resource Exploration and Environmental
   Science (REES), Ordos, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 14-16, 2017},
Abstract = {Sulfate reducing bacteria (SRB) was isolated from urban soil and applied
   for the remediation of heavy metals pollution from acid mine drainage.
   The morphology and physiological characteristics (e.g. pH and heavy
   metals tolerance) of SRB was investigated. The SRB was gram-negative
   bacteria, long rod with slight curve, cell size 0.5x (1.5-2.0) mu m. The
   pH of medium had significant effect on SRB growth and the efficiency of
   sulfate reduction, and it showed that the suitable pH range was 5-9 and
   SRB could not survive at pH less than 4. The maximum tolerance of Fe
   (II), Zn (II), Cd (II), and Cu (II) under acidic condition (pH 5.0) was
   about 600 mg/L, 150 mg/L, 25 mg/L and 25 mg/L, respectively. The result
   indicated that SRB isolated in this study could be used for the
   bioremediation of acid mine drainage (pH>4) within the heavy metals
   concentrations tolerance.},
