   Grigore T Popa Univ Med \& Pharmacy, ELECTR NETWORK, NOV 18-19, 2021},
Organization = {IEEE; Grigore T Popa Univ Med \& Pharmacy, Fac Med Bioengineering; SRBM;
   IEEE Romanian Sect; IEEE EMB; IEEE Romania Sect; Inst Informatica
   Teoretica; Romanian Soc Med Bioengineering; Romanian Acad, Iasi Branch,
   Inst Comp Sci; IEEE EMB Romania Chapter; IEEE EMC Romania Chapter; IEEE
   Signal Proc Romania Chapter; IEEE SMC Romania Chapter},
Abstract = {Predicting and recognizing emotions is becoming an important
   preoccupation for the medical field, but also in areas such as
   organizational wellbeing, psychotherapy or neuromarketing. Biological
   signals are powerful markers for emotions and stress, as shown by
   previous research and the rising field of affective computing. This
   paper presents the design and implementation of a strategy to classify
   emotions and emotional dimensions by using heart rate variability (HRV)
   and electrodermal activity (EDA) as physiological indicators, after
   researching multiple potential markers for emotional states. A new
   dataset was created during the presented research and machine learning
   techniques were used to assess whether the two chosen bio-signals are
   strong indicators for human emotions. Results indicate that the design
   of the strategy is a successful one, with obtained accuracies of up to
   86\% being aligned with results from other papers, while the sensors
   used are highly affordable and accessible.},
