Abstract = {To what extent do differences in biological sex and psychological gender
   identity influence affective reactions to different genres of film? In
   order to address this question, this investigation examined the impact
   of sex and gender role self-perceptions on viewers' responses to
   neutral, melodramatic, and violent plm segments. Working with a
   predominantly Caucasian population (93\% Caucasian) at a southeastern
   university, the results emphasize the importance of sex and gender role
   self-perceptions on viewers' affective responses to media entertainment
