Abstract = {In two profiling experiments and one grouping experiment, panelists
   evaluated orange drinks in order to measure the effects of design
   variables, especially color, on basic tastes as well as on more
   consumer-like attributes such as flavor strength and naturalness,
   Naturalness was increased in one experiment by lowering degrees Brix or
   increasing quinine HCl, Low sweet-sour ratios were generally perceived
   as more natural Pectin had no effect on naturalness. Flavor strength was
   increased consistently by augmenting levels of quinine HCl, sucrose,
   citric acid or degrees Brix. Addition of Cochineal Red increased
   sweetness and flavor strength but decreased the perception of
   naturalness far the aromas studied.},
