   SEP 09-13, 2002},
Organization = {Int Assoc Housing Sci},
Abstract = {Of the 09 to September 13, 2002, the IAHS will organize the XXXe world
   convention on the lodging. This demonstration will be very important for
   the future of the inhabited space.
   In the hope to contribute on the initiative of the IAHS, I would like to
   make you part of my aspirations and my conception of the space lived in
   the farming society. Since we long all for new policies and new styles
   of lodgings and after having analyzed the successes and the failures of
   the past and to have thought about the problems that put themselves to
   the possible evolutions, I decided to participate in this convention
   with a scientist's ambition so that we constructed a best world
   together.
   It is about examining the possibilities of a development spatially more
   adapted. It is also about re-establishing a balance of the investments
   and the scientific investigating between the urban and farming
   preoccupations. In definitive, it is about adapting the instruments of
   analysis and projection of the lodging to the farming environment. It
   will permit us to correct the urban perception of the production centers
   structure.
   The urbanization that marks the traditional farming space strongly
   misled an important spatial restructuring. It is about measuring the
   size of the transformations of it and to give itself/themselves the
   scientific means that will permit to act in the common sense.
   The societies are various by their cultures, their ability and their
   values that they must carry through the world thanks to the meetings and
   to the dialogues as those that will cause this XXXe convention of the
   IAHS.
   An architect's future depends on his/her/its architectural oeuvres: more
   he/it will have the creativeness; more his/her/its profession will be
   valorised. An architecture that affirms itself sees itself constructive
   and adapted to his/her/its society and his/her/its time.},
