Note = {9th Conference on Interdisciplinary Problems in Environmental Protection
   and Engineering (EKO-DOK), Boguszow Gorce, POLAND, APR 23-25, 2017},
Abstract = {The main task of the stormwater drainage system (SDS) is a safe drainage
   of rainwater and snowmelt from the urban area to the receiver. The flow
   of rain water in the drainage pipes is directly related with the
   formation of sediments in the whole stormwater system. In addition,
   pollutants from land runoff get adsorbed to the sediments. The sludge is
   mainly formed in those elements of SDS, wherein the flow conditions
   allow for sedimentation. This article provides an overview of the
   literature concerning the characteristics of sediments from SDS, with a
   particular focus on heavy metals in sediments deposited in the urban
   catchment area.},
