Abstract = {Our aim is to develop an assessment procedure, independent of language
   and speech production, to test young deaf children on the perceptual
   capacities involved in the normal early development of speech
   processing. Based on the Visual Reinforcement Infant Speech
   Discrimination procedure, our version of the procedure can be used to
   test discrimination of speech contrasts as well as categorization of
   various speech stimuli. In the present study, we focus on the perception
