   together Engineering and Economics (ICEE), Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, MAY
   16-17, 2019},
Organization = {Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ Porto, Sch Econ \& Management; UP, Ctr Econ
   \& Finance; CentroAlgoritmi},
Abstract = {Air pollution is an environmental risk factor being an important cause
   of disease, for which cities and living standards within cities
   contributes a lot. This paper tries to analyze the effect of urban air
   pollution in 24 German cities for the years 2007, 2010 and 2013 for
   which there was available data. We start by analyzing the relative
   behavior of their eco-efficiency (using a new measure), by determining
   efficiency scores. Afterwards, a fractional regression model was applied
   to infer about factors able to influence these scores. Results evidence
   a significant effect on technical efficiency of excess particulate
   matter (PM10), the average temperature, the average concentration of
   nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and rainfall. Intervenctions to reduce urban air
   pollution can be accomplished on different regulatory levels, leading
   also to synergistic effects (decrease climate change effects and noise).},
