Title = {Influence of land consolidation on biomass and ecological environment},
Booktitle = {PROGRESS IN ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY, VOL I},
Year = {2007},
Pages = {85-90},
Note = {International Symposium on Environmental Science and Technology,
   Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 13-16, 2007},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol},
Abstract = {The biomass change, resulted from integrated effect of environmental
   factors, is one of the symbols of community succession and of regional
   exhibition of, global change. The succession of natural ecosystem
   reflects the regional response mechanism of global change, and the
   succession of man-made ecosystem reflects the contribution of human
   activities to global change. So the driving force of biomass change is
   different between the natural and man-made ecosystems. Land
   consolidation is the adjustment of regional land use pattern, being
   constituted of 4. engineering systems such as land leveling engineering,
   farmland irrigation works engineering, road construction engineering,
   and protection forest engineering. Land consolidation changes the types
   and spatial patterns of regional ecosystems to form a manpower
   succession of ecosystem. Following the succession, the structures and
   functions of ecosystern are changed accordingly, of which one of the
   representations is the biomass change of regional biocenosis. And the
   biomass change determines the influence of regional biocenosis on
   regional environment. The measure and calculation of biomass
   fore-and-aft land consolidation are worked out by the sample plot method
   in terms of arbor, shrub, herbage plants and crops. The result shows
   that the biomass is increased 580 t after land consolidation, meaning
   the impression of land consolidation is remarkable in general. The
   results of monomial analysis are as follows: (1) the biomass of sparse
   forest is not changed fore-and aft land consolidation, but its ratio of
   biomass is reduced by 2.5\%, and its ecological influence is slightly
   weakened; (2) the biomass of man-made forest and sparse forest is
   increased by 6\% after land consolidation, hence, the total ecological
   influence of woodland is enhanced; (3) the ecological influence of waste
   grassplot disappeared with the disappearance of its biomas after land
   consolidation; (4) the total biomass of dry-land crops is all most not
   changed, but its influence is reduced by 17.87\%; (5) the total biomass
   of rice has the largest growth with an increase of 477.94 t after land
   consolidation, accounting for 82.4\% of the total increased amount, and
   its total ecological influence is up to 14.12\%. The results also show:
   (1) the structure and function of regional ecosystem will be changed by
   land consolidation, and the biomass will be changed accordingly; (2)
   marked ecological influence will be induced from the biomass change, not
   only the natural ecosystem, but also the human ecosystem.},
