Year = {2019},
Volume = {344},
Note = {5th International Conference on Water Resource and Environment (WRE) /
   1st International Conference on Advances in Civil and Ecological
   Engineering Research (ACEER), Macau Univ Sci \& Technol, Macao, PEOPLES
   R CHINA, JUN 16-19, 2019},
Abstract = {In recent years, urban waterlogging has become a stubborn disease in
   major cities such as Beijing, Shanghai, Nanjing, Wuhan, and Xi'an. The
   city's sea view is mainly due to the extreme torrential rain that
   exceeds the urban design and drainage capacity. Therefore, in view of
   the problem of domestic rains and inland ``Seeing the sea{''}, this
   paper takes the typical heavy rain in Wuhan as an example. The typical
   rainstorm frequency analysis methods in the municipal department and the
   water conservancy department are using to measure rainstorm under
   different sampling conditions. The design frequencies of different
   grades rainstorm has been analyzed in municipal and water conservancy
   systems. While that is expected to definite the design frequency of
   different grades of heavy rain in municipal and water conservancy
   systems from the quantitative level. The matching relationship is
   expected between the rainstorm frequency analysis results of the two
   methods, which provide data support for the design standards of flood
   control and drainage in the construction of sponge cities.},
