   International-Society-for-the-Study-of-Behavioural-Development, nanjing,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 15-17, 2009},
Organization = {Int Soc Study Behav Dev; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {This experiment mainly investigated the processing of attachment-related
   emotional information and non-attachment-related emotional information.
   This experiment adopted the ERP technique and set tip three experimental
   conditions: attachment-related emotion, non-attachment-related emotion
   and neutral conditions. Between the 450ms-700ms after the stimulus
   appeared, the main effect of the three conditions was significant F(2,
   68) = 19.039, P < 0.05, epsilon = 0.359). The interaction between the
   three condition and left-right brain hemisphere was also significant
   F(2, 68) = 11,575, P < 0.05, epsilon = 0.254. The interaction between
   the three condition and frontal-central-parietal brain area was also
   significant F(4, 136) = 13.137, P < 0.05, epsilon = 0.279. The results
   supported the hypothesis that attachment-related emotional information
   can activate the attachment system more pronounced than the
   non-attachment-related emotional information and neutral information,
   especially on the right hemisphere.},
