   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {This paper describes the development and use of thematic maps for an
   integrated study of a large number of cut slopes and adjacent natural
   terrain within two urban areas of Hong Kong Island. The study was
   carried out following two fatal landslides of slopes within these areas
   in August 1995. The study has identified a number of slopes with
   geological features similar to those at the two fatal landslide sites.
   The results of the study support the use of geographic information
   systems (GIS) for evaluating all existing data sources in a regional
   context when assessing slope stability potential.},
