   MONDUZZI EDITORE},
Title = {Awareness,perception and risk behaviors of drug users in the prisons},
Booktitle = {XIV INTERNATIONAL AIDS CONFERENCE: SOCIAL SCIENCES},
Year = {2002},
Pages = {331-335},
Note = {14th International AIDS Conference, BARCELONA, SPAIN, JUL 07-12, 2002},
Organization = {Univ N Carolina; Gen Clin Res Ctr; UNC Ctr AIDS Res; Natl Inst Hlth;
   Swiss Natl AIDS Res Program; Bristol-Myers Squibb Co; Boehringer
   Ingelheim; GlaxoWellcome Res \& Dev, HIV Antiviral Res},
Abstract = {The aim of this study is to determine the awareness, risk perception and
   risk taking behavior of prisoners who use drugs and to implement
   effective health education programs in the prisons.
   Qualitative data collected using key informant interviews, Focus group
   discussions and in-depth interviews.
   In-depth Interviews revealed 28\% of the participants were drug users
   with median age of 24. Median of drug use starting age was 21 (range
   13-34). Median number of years drug use was 5 (range 1- 14 years). 37\%
   completed high school and 33\% dropped out of school. 71\% of the drug
   users consumed oral and intravenous drugs and 75\% of them always-shared
   needles. 38\% of them said they had casual partners and 30\% had
   frequent visits to sex workers. None of them ever used condoms. Only
   14\% perceived that they might have HIV. Awareness on HIV/AIDS was very
   limited with many misconceptions.
   Drug use and male-to-male sex is not openly discussed but ``happens{''}.
   This study shows a rather high rate of risk behaviors and low level of
   knowledge.},
