Abstract = {``Tram-train{''} systems carry out the integration of an urban tramway
   with the surrounding railway network, by means of light rail vehicles
   often provided with special wheel profiles in order to fit both grooved
   and flat-bottomed rails. This paper aims to compare the dynamic
   behaviour of atypical Light Rail Vehicle (LRV) provided with these
   ``tram-train{''} wheel profiles with the dynamics of the same LRV
   provided with an heavy railway standard wheel profile by modelling, in a
   multi-body simulation environment, the run on railway tracks of a
   virtual vehicle provided with these two wheel profiles.},
