   cities. While urban central areas are usually endowed with a multitude
   of green spaces, they are also the areas that are most prone to the
   undesirable effects of growth and urbanisation. Planning of sustainable
   cities serves as a fundamental catalyst for change, improving
   environmental quality of the natural and built environments, and
   upgrading conditions for development of green architecture. This paper
